  "purpose": "Rung P4b (heredity carrier channels, G1b): judge Cells' own physics (resolved_pump_tissue@3 with network channel populations) on the rung-1 mammal default world: Kir2.1 (1e-8 m/s), Na leak and K leak active from INIT; NaV1.2 (2.5e-7 m/s) switched on at SIM start. INIT rests near -34.2 mV; SIM ramps Vm about +6.2 mV over 35 ms (0.15-0.19 mV/ms) as NaV1.2 activates and inactivates. Against the plain-BETSE case parity-p4b-channels-20261110-01/derive-01/betse-reference/p4b-kir-navsim-dense (general network with only these channels, no biomolecules). Tolerances by the pinned method (3 x the sum of measured terms; every cell-ion field term propagated through the reference emulator).",
