    "step_order_rule": {
      "rule": "BETSE's step term is (10/9) |x(dt) - x(dt/10)| (emulator, SIM chained) if the observed order on p4b-kir-navsim-dense (dt, dt/10, dt/100) is within 0.9-1.1 for Vm and every cell ion but P in INIT and SIM; otherwise |x(dt) - x(dt/100)| for every step term in both P4b cases, and the compact-ECM-face and gate-once terms at dt/100 instead of dt/10 (lead, 10 November). A failed check counts as the fallback.",
      "check": "/mnt/workspaces/Cells/parity-p4b-channels-20261110-01/derive-01/emulator/order_check_p4b-kir-navsim-dense.json",
      "outcome": "step terms (10/9)|dt1 - dt10| in every P4b case"
    },
    "field_terms": "cell-ion, Vm and ECM field terms propagated through the BETSE-order emulator (validation/betse/field_propagation.py --runner network; boltzmann, vpatch and both on the (1 ms, 0.1 ms) and (0.5 ms, 0.05 ms) blind layouts; max over the six pairs). The X_ext per-volt heuristic is not used. The ECM Boltzmann response of Cells' own exterior field (field_layouts) stays as in P4."
  },
  "observable_mapping": "BETSE vm in this world is cell charge / (cm * sum mem_sa), uniform within a cell (Phi_b = 0; v_env not subtracted; sim.py:2029). Cells vm_ave = Q_cell / sum C_patch with C_patch = cm * mem_sa, broadcast to membranes for vm. Patch voltages and exterior potentials are diag_* arrays, reported only. Boundary-ring ECM sites are excluded: BETSE resets them each step, the resolved model holds them as reservoirs.",
  "notes": [
    "Reported only: venv_time (BETSE's screened, smoothed estimate has no Cells counterpart) and Cells diag_* arrays.",
    "Gate open fractions are not in the comparison layout and are not judged.",
    "Leave-one-out plain-BETSE cases: parity-p4b-channels-20261110-01/derive-01/betse-reference/p4b-kir-navsim-no-<channel>-dense."
